{{!
    @template tool_vae/positioning_line

    One line of a positioning of the structure: its status in bold, who wrote it and when, its reason, and the reason of an
    alert when there is one. The parts touch: the template holds on one logical line, each break carried by a comment.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\positioning_line. The template holds no logic.
    Every value is escaped (double braces) except two keys:
    * reasonhtml - the reason, drawn by format_text() as plain text (the core escapes it)
    * alerthtml - the reason of the alert, drawn the same way

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * status - string, the status, with the day of the decision and the day it stands until for a certification
    * signature - string, who wrote the line and when
    * reasonhtml - string, HTML of the core: the reason
    * alert - object or null: label (the words before the reason of the alert), alerthtml (HTML of the core)

    Example context (json):
    {
        "status": "certified by the structure (decided on 2026-11-04) - stands until 2027-11-04",
        "signature": "Dana Direction, Wednesday, 4 November 2026, 10:12 AM",
        "reasonhtml": "Two situations seen on the ward.",
        "alert": {"label": "Reason of the alert", "alerthtml": "Second competency seen next week."}
    }
}}
<div class="ms-3 mb-2"><div class="small"><strong>{{status}}</strong> {{signature}}</div><div>{{{reasonhtml}}}</div>{{!
}}{{#alert}}<div class="small"><em>{{label}} : </em>{{{alerthtml}}}</div>{{/alert}}</div>
